#### 2. File to Modify: `present.py` (Markdown Parsers)

Ensure that:
1. `_md_to_html` (or the `markdown` third-party module) correctly processes code blocks with class `language-mermaid` and translates them to `<div class="mermaid">` tags.
2. It detects images in the markdown `![alt](url)` and wraps them in `<div class="image-wrapper"><img class="report-img" src="url" alt="alt"/><div class="image-fallback"></div></div>`.
3. Validates against placeholder leaks.

##### Python Implementation:

```python
def _md_to_html_enhanced(md_text: str) -> str:
    """
    Enhanced basic parser converting markdown elements, handling custom Mermaid divs
    and wrapper structures for images.
    """
    if _HAVE_MD:
        import markdown as _md
        # Basic markdown conversion
        html = _md.markdown(md_text, extensions=["tables", "fenced_code"])
    else:
        html = _md_to_html(md_text) # Fallback basic parser

    # Post-process to translate code block tag structures to Mermaid divs
    html = re.sub(
        r'<pre><code class="language-mermaid">(.*?)</code></pre>',
        r'<div class="mermaid">\1</div>',
        html,
        flags=re.DOTALL
    )
    
    # Translate standard markdown images to premium wrappers with fallbacks
    html = re.sub(
        r'<img alt="(.*?)" src="(.*?)"[^>]*>',
        r'<div class="image-wrapper"><img class="report-img" src="\2" alt="\1"/><div class="image-fallback"></div></div>',
        html
    )
    
    return html
